      "description": "Given finite filtrations F, G, F', G' (weight tables on a finite simplex support) and a clock value t in [0,1], the certifier computes the actual distance between the two synchronized interpolants, the convex Busemann bound, and the curvature slack. A non-negative slack is a per-instance certificate of Busemann non-positive curvature (Theorem eInterleavingDist_lerp_bicombing). Each distance is a maximum of absolute weight gaps via the isometry formula, so a single certification runs in time linear in the number of simplices in the support.",
      "pseudocode": "function bicombing_slack(F, G, Fp, Gp, t):\\n    require 0 <= t <= 1\\n    L  <- lerp(F, G, t)          # weight (1-t) wF + t wG\\n    Lp <- lerp(Fp, Gp, t)        # weight (1-t) wFp + t wGp\\n    lhs <- max over sigma of | L[sigma] - Lp[sigma] |\\n    dFFp <- max over sigma of | F[sigma]  - Fp[sigma] |\\n    dGGp <- max over sigma of | G[sigma]  - Gp[sigma] |\\n    rhs <- (1 - t) * dFFp + t * dGGp\\n    return (lhs, rhs, rhs - lhs)   # slack >= 0 certifies the inequality",
      "code": "from itertools import combinations\nfrom typing import Dict, FrozenSet, Hashable, List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nSimplex = FrozenSet[Hashable]\nFiltration = Dict[Simplex, float]\n\n\ndef interleaving_distance(F: Filtration, G: Filtration) -> float:\n    \"\"\"d(F, G) = max over simplices of |w_F(sigma) - w_G(sigma)| (isometry formula).\"\"\"\n    keys = set(F) | set(G)\n    return max(abs(F.get(s, 0.0) - G.get(s, 0.0)) for s in keys)\n\n\ndef lerp(F: Filtration, G: Filtration, t: float) -> Filtration:\n    \"\"\"Geodesic interpolation of weights; requires 0 <= t <= 1.\"\"\"\n    assert 0.0 <= t <= 1.0\n    keys = set(F) | set(G)\n    return {s: (1.0 - t) * F.get(s, 0.0) + t * G.get(s, 0.0) for s in keys}\n\n\ndef bicombing_slack(\n    F: Filtration, G: Filtration, Fp: Filtration, Gp: Filtration, t: float\n) -> Tuple[float, float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Certify the convex geodesic bicombing inequality at parameter t.\n\n    Returns (lhs, rhs, slack) where\n        lhs   = d(lerp(F,G,t), lerp(Fp,Gp,t)),\n        rhs   = (1 - t) d(F, Fp) + t d(G, Gp),\n        slack = rhs - lhs >= 0  (Busemann non-positive curvature).\n    Complexity: O(|support|) per call.\n    \"\"\"\n    lhs = interleaving_distance(lerp(F, G, t), lerp(Fp, Gp, t))\n    rhs = (1.0 - t) * interleaving_distance(F, Fp) + t * interleaving_distance(G, Gp)\n    return lhs, rhs, rhs - lhs\n"
